From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:59:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-consys: log each STP resend

A long A2DP stream had 40 ACK timeouts and the controller reported more
completed packets than the host sent, in groups the size of a resend.
The halt line only gives totals, so nothing says when they happened or
what the link was doing. It also showed one unsolicited WMT message,
keeping only the first.

Log each timeout with the frames outstanding and queued, the peer's ACK
and the frame counts, and each unsolicited WMT message, limited by rate.
The time lines up with a Bluetooth trace, and the received count shows if
the firmware kept talking while its ACK stayed put.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
index c56e587b1..6bbef6bca 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c
@@ -1849,14 +1849,24 @@ static irqreturn_t mt6797_stp_irq(int irq, void *data)
 static void mt6797_stp_tick(struct timer_list *t)
 {
 	struct mt6797_stp *s = timer_container_of(s, t, tick);
+	struct device *dev = container_of(s, struct mt6797_consys, stp)->dev;
 	unsigned long flags;
+	unsigned int timeouts;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&s->lock, flags);
 	if (!s->stopped) {
+		timeouts = s->engine.tx_timeouts;
 		if (stp_engine_tick(&s->engine, jiffies,
 				    msecs_to_jiffies(MT6797_STP_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS))) {
 			mt6797_stp_stop_locked(s);
 		} else {
+			if (s->engine.tx_timeouts != timeouts)
+				dev_info_ratelimited(dev,
+						     "STP resend %u: try=%u unacked=%u pending=%u queued=%u peer-ack=%u tx=%u rx=%u\n",
+						     s->engine.tx_timeouts, s->engine.retries,
+						     s->engine.unacked, s->engine.link.tx_pending,
+						     s->engine.count, s->engine.link.peer_ack,
+						     s->engine.tx_frames, s->engine.rx_frames);
 			if (s->engine.resync_owed)
 				mt6797_stp_pump(s);
 			mod_timer(&s->tick, jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(MT6797_STP_TICK_MS));
@@ -1894,6 +1904,9 @@ static int mt6797_stp_wmt_rx(void *context, const unsigned char *payload,
 		complete(&s->wmt_done);
 		return 0;
 	}
+	dev_info_ratelimited(container_of(s, struct mt6797_consys, stp)->dev,
+			     "STP unsolicited WMT: %*ph\n",
+			     min_t(int, length, sizeof(s->wmt_first)), payload);
 	if (!s->wmt_unsolicited++) {
 		memcpy(s->wmt_first, payload, min_t(unsigned int, length, sizeof(s->wmt_first)));
 		s->wmt_first_length = length;
-- 
2.43.0

